    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T21:52:15Z",
    "body": "Label back to needs-rework: the head is still 7e39726, the commit the review flagged, so the blocker stands. `pockets_of` doesn't check mesh winding, so an inside-out mesh is recognised as one closed pocket the size of the part's outline, floor at the base, and `detect_pockets` with `create` would make a Pocket that cuts the whole footprint. Fix: run the #387 body-winding verdict (`pick/winding.rs`) first, refuse an inside-out or open body by name, and pin it with a reversed cube and a reversed pocket block. Push that and it gets a fresh review.",
